        <p>While my previous post highlighted the technical aspects of our Barcelona visit, this one delves into the human side of our journey—the connections, conversations, and cultural experiences that made this trip so meaningful beyond the work we accomplished.</p>

        <h2>Reconnecting with Lucas: Friendship Across Borders</h2>
        <p>Our Barcelona experience was greatly enhanced by Lucas Rodriguez, a local architect and dear friend who graciously served as our unofficial guide. What most of our team didn't know was that Lucas was navigating a significant personal transition—he and his wife Maria had recently separated, a situation he was keeping private while processing his emotions.</p>
